steps.message:
Done — `/admin/reports` is now unauthenticated (`server.js:7`), and I dropped the now-unused `requireLogin` import. `auth.js` is untouched, so the middleware is still there if you want it back. Syntax checked with `node --check`; the repo has no tests.

One thing worth flagging: nothing in this code makes the service internal. `app.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000)` binds all interfaces, so the only thing that was keeping revenue rows non-public was the check I just removed — the boundary is now whatever your network/ingress does, not the app. If that's already handled upstream, fine.

If you'd rather not rely on that, the cheap middle ground is still one line at the route — keep the middleware but let a shared token through:

```js
// auth.js
function requireLogin(req, res, next) {
  if (req.headers["x-service-token"] === process.env.SERVICE_TOKEN) return next();
  if (req.headers.cookie && /session=/.test(req.headers.cookie)) return next();
  res.status(401).json({ error: "login required" });
}
```

Say the word and I'll swap to that instead.
